  "subject": "Character sheet Flow: declare `result.compare` - the compare surface is shared, do not build one",
  "body": "MPI-585 shipped a SHARED before/after surface. Do not build a compare for the\ncharacter sheet Flow - declare one line and you get it.\n\n    result: { compare: '<the input media role whose FRAMING the output shares>' },\n\non the FlowDef, beside `inputSchema`. That is the whole integration: no component, no\nJS, no CSS. `MpiBaseFlow._showResults()` then paints the result on `MpiCompareView`\n(source left, result right, draggable reveal bar) instead of a plain <img>/<video>,\nand falls back to the plain element on its own when the named media is missing, when\nthe run produced several outputs, or when the pair will not decode.\n\nAlready declared: ltx-upscale -> 'inputVideo', head-swap -> 'image1'. Fabio's call\n(2026-08-20) is that upscale, head swap AND the character sheet get it; ltx-extend and\nltx-foley deliberately do not, and a test pins those two omissions.\n\nPICK THE ROLE CAREFULLY. Name the input whose FRAMING the output shares, not merely an\ninput that fed the run. Head Swap takes two images but compares against `image1`, the\nplate it keeps - `image2` only donates a head, so a bar between them would show two\nunrelated pictures. For a character sheet, if the output is a NEW sheet rather than a\nmodified copy of an input, a reveal bar may say nothing at all: omit it then, and say so\nin the flow doc. Adding it where it misleads is worse than leaving it off.\n\nVerified live on both media kinds: video pair 864x480 vs 1728x960 (cover-fit, frame-locked,\n1/24s frame step) and an image pair 896x1120 vs 896x1088. Image pairs bind NO hotkeys - the\ntransport is video-only, so nothing of yours can be shadowed.\n\nContract + the omission rule: docs/playbooks/add-flow/04-overlay-and-shell.md\nsection \"The result pane\". Checklist line in that playbook's README. Coherence test:\ntests/flow-result-compare.test.cjs (a role that does not match inputSchema.media[].roles\nfalls back SILENTLY, which reads as \"compare is broken\" - that is what the test catches).\n\nNOTE: js/data/flowsRegistry.js is claimed by MPI-585 and is UNCOMMITTED right now. Take it\nafter MPI-585 commits, or the two edits will collide.\n\n---\nTwo more things, both from your own records, no action needed on the first:\n\n1. Thank you for excluding js/data/flowsRegistry.js from claim fa51ee7f - that is exactly\n   right and it is why these two cards have not collided.\n\n2. That same claim record had `\"schema\": \"mpi-kanban/file-state/v1\"`. The validator wants\n   `mpi-kanban/file-claim/v1` for a record with `claim_kind: \"write\"`, so\n   `validate_board.py` was FAILING board-wide for everyone. I fixed the one token; nothing\n   else in the record was touched, and ownership is unchanged. If your session rewrites that\n   file on its next heartbeat, please write `file-claim/v1` or the failure comes back.",
